<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Continental yr profit 11.4 mln punts.</title>
<headline>Irish Continental yr profit 11.4 mln punts.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to October 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		44.2		   vs 42.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.6		    vs 3.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.4		    vs 4.5</p>
<p>Profit before tax,</p>
<p> and exceptionals	 11.4		   vs n/a</p>
<p> Turnover		   127.17		 vs 116.42</p>
<p> Operating costs	  110.63		 vs 104.00</p>
<p>Operating profit</p>
<p>  before exceptionals   16.54		  vs 12.41</p>
<p> Net interest payable   3.73		   vs 2.90</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	   10.54		  vs 11.03</p>
<p> Taxation		   0.65 credit	  vs 0.24 charge</p>
<p> Profit attributable    11.20		  vs 10.79</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish Continental Group said on Wednesday that it had made an exceptional provision of 1.60 million Irish pounds to reduce the carrying value of its investment in Bell Lines to nil.</p>
<p>The group's share of the results of Bell, its 25 percent associated company, was a loss of 1.59 million punts in the period compared with a profit of 0.76 million the previous year.</p>
<p>ICG also reported an exceptional credit of 0.71 million compared with an exceptional charge of 0.38 million the previous year and a profit of 0.20 million on disposal of assets against a profit of 1.14 a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
